  "project_description_general": "The SERCOVA Project aims to enhance forest management, conserve biodiversity, and improve the resilience and wellbeing of Indigenous People and Local Communities (IPLC) through a series of targeted activities. The primary goals are to reduce greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions, conserve High Conservation Value (HCV) species, and improve the livelihoods and climate resilience of IPLCs. The project employs a multi-faceted approach that includes forest rehabilitation, biodiversity monitoring, climate adaptation training, and the promotion of climate-smart livelihood options. Special emphasis is placed on prioritizing vulnerable groups and ensuring inclusive participation in decision-making processes.",
  "project_description_general_en": "",
  "project_description_special": "SERCOVA Project is designed to deliver the project goal through a series of objectives, including below:\n1. Reduce GHG Emissions and Improve Forest Management\na. Implemented Forest Management (IFM) practices.\nb. Convert logging activities to protected forest activities.\nc. Conduct regular forest and fire patrols.\n\n2. Conserve Biodiversity and HCV Species\na. Identify and monitor HCV species.\nb. Develop and implement biodiversity management plans.\nc. Reduce threats from illegal wildlife trade and hunting.\n\n3. Enhance IPLC Resilience and Wellbeing\na. Provide climate adaptation training.\nb. Promote climate-smart agriculture and fisheries.\nc. Improve livelihood options through community enterprise development.\n\n4. Prioritize Vulnerable Groups\na. Ensure health and education services prioritize vulnerable groups.\nb. Facilitate inclusive participation in decision-making processes.\nc. Develop social safeguards to ensure transparent and just project implementation.",
  "project_description_special_en": "",
